From 662568cfcfda48b6ef186c774df4f4e4ab043588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:37:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 45/47] darwin: drop the no_quarantine cask argument

Homebrew deprecated the --no-quarantine switch, which bypasses
Gatekeeper, and has since removed it
(https://github.com/Homebrew/brew/issues/20755).  The Homebrew that
nix-homebrew pins, 7.0.15, rejects it as an invalid option, so brew
bundle fails to install a cask that is not installed yet.  Installed
casks are unaffected, because brew bundle does not pass cask arguments
when it upgrades them.  Without the argument, new casks are quarantined
like any other download, and macOS checks them on their first launch.
Homebrew has stopped supporting casks that fail Gatekeeper, so this
should not block any cask it ships.
---
 systems/darwin/default.nix | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/systems/darwin/default.nix b/systems/darwin/default.nix
index cfc274e..08ff754 100644
--- a/systems/darwin/default.nix
+++ b/systems/darwin/default.nix
@@ -150,7 +150,6 @@
 
   homebrew = {
     enable = true;
-    caskArgs.no_quarantine = true;
     global.brewfile = true;
     masApps = { };
     casks = [
-- 
2.56.1

